$DIR/main.p:9:13: the move check of this function did not settle after 2000 passes over its body: the compiler's limit on the number of passes
    The program goes past a limit of this compiler. The parser accepts
    expressions, statements and types nested up to 100000 levels deep, the type
    checker up to its own nesting limit, which is lower when its stack runs
    short, and the move check makes at most 2000 passes over one function's body
    before what it knows at each loop and label settles. The message names the
    limit. The program is not wrong, but this compiler cannot build it as
    written.
    Split the deep expression or type into named parts:
        a := f(g(x))
        b := h(a)
    (see "Implementation limits" in the Plutonium spec, section 21.4)
    (run "pluto explain E9002" for a longer explanation)
